# Explicit @Unknown annotation: should produce an Info diagnostic (T011)
# The type checker detects explicit @Unknown and emits Info instead of Warn
#
# NOTE: T010 ("inferred type is Unknown") was intentionally removed from === warn.
# Both T010 and T011 fire for this input, but warning ORDER is non-deterministic across runs
# (the type checker's diagnostic list is not sorted before output). Using a single-line
# substring match ("explicit @Unknown annotation") is stable: it matches T011 regardless
# of whether T010 appears before or after it in the actual output. Asserting the exact
# T010 line caused intermittent failures when the order flipped between runs.
[f: [fn@Unknown [let x] x]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x)})

=== warn
inferred type is Unknown — consider adding a type annotation
explicit @Unknown annotation — type is not statically known
